/MSFT/Policy/Config/onent16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOneNote~L_OneNoteOptions~L_Editing/L_IncludelinktosourcewhenpastingfromtheInternet","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-onent16v2"},{"key":"L_OneNoteTextPrediction","name":"OneNote text prediction (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting controls whether users will see and be able to accept text predictions when writing notes in English in OneNote.\n\nIf you enable or don't configure this policy setting, users will see and be able to accept predicted text by using the Tab key or right arrow key while writing their notes. Or they can simply keep typing to ignore the predicted text.\n\nIf you disable this policy setting, users will not be able to see or accept text predictions while writing notes.\n\nNote: This policy setting only applies to subscription versions of Office, such as Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/onent16v5~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOneNote~L_OneNoteOptions~L_Editing/L_OneNoteTextPrediction","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-onent16v5"},{"key":"L_ShowPasteOptionsbuttons","name":"Show Paste Options buttons (User)","type":"enum","description":"Checks/Unchecks the corresponding UI option.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/onent16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOneNote~L_OneNoteOptions~L_Editing/L_ShowPasteOptionsbuttons","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-onent16v2"},{"key":"L_Turnoffautocalculator","name":"Turn off auto calculator (User)","type":"enum","description":"This option turns on/off the auto calculator functionality.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/onent16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOneNote~L_OneNoteOptions~L_Editing/L_Turnoffautocalculator","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-onent16v2"},{"key":"L_TurnOffLinkCreationWith","name":"Turn off link creation with [[ ]] (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting allows you to turn off link creation with [[ ]]. OneNote allows users to automatically create links by putting [[ ]] around a term. OneNote will then automatically create a new page in that section and create a link on that text.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting, users will not be able to use [[ ]] to create a link and a new page.\n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, OneNote will automatically create links when users use [[ ]].","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/onent16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOneNote~L_OneNoteOptions~L_Editing/L_TurnOffLinkCreationWith","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-onent16v2"}],"source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/configuration-service-provider-reference"}
